<%# One thing being judged, framed so the evidence and the verdict are on screen
    together: the source pinned (left of the fields on a wide screen, above them on
    a phone), the body scrolling beside it, the decision bar always in reach.
    Render with `render layout:` — the block is the body.

    `actions` is pre-rendered markup rather than a second block because the bar sits
    OUTSIDE the scrolling body; i18n inside the block must use ABSOLUTE keys (see
    the page_header gotcha). `source_attrs` lands on the source pane, which the
    caller fills: evidence a client holds in memory only (a capture's poster, never
    uploaded for storage) is written into the pane from the browser rather than
    passed as `source`. %>
<%# locals: (id:, actions:, source: nil, frame_class: nil, frame_attrs: {}, source_attrs: {}) %>
<%= tag.div id: id, class: ["review-card", frame_class], **frame_attrs do %>
  <%= tag.div source, class: "review-card__source", **source_attrs %>
  <div class="review-card__body"><%= yield %></div>
  <%= actions %>
<% end %>
